# Authorize master pushes in GitHub Desktop

When the user asks to push or update GitHub master:

- Bump the Admin version first. Run `npm run version:bump`, then add and commit `src/ros-version.json` if it changed (same commit as the work, or a follow-up commit if the work is already committed). Admin reads that file at Vite build time. Skipping it freezes the label (this is not IDE vs Agent — both must bump).
- Commit first if needed, then start `git push` so they can authorize.
- Force the GitHub Desktop / account picker. Use `GCM_INTERACTIVE=always` so cached credentials do not push silently.
- The Cursor Auto-review card is not a substitute. They must see GitHub Desktop and pick their account.
- Do not tell them to push themselves instead of starting the push.
